# Domain Model – RoomLight

## Overview

RoomLight has rooms, lights, modes and a main controller. The controller sets the lights and makes sure all rooms are updated.

## Entities

### Controller
- controls all rooms
- stores the main lighting setup
- updates rooms when settings change

### Room
- a hotel room
- has one light
- can have default or custom settings

### Light
- belongs to a room
- can be on or off
- has a brightness level
- uses a mode

### Mode
- tells the light how to behave
- examples: night mode, reading mode, energy saving mode

## Relationships

- One controller manages many rooms (1 → n)  
- One room has one light (1 → 1)  
- One light uses one mode (1 → 1)  
- One mode can be used by many lights (1 → n)

